==============================================================================
D. ALL Stormer pairs as unit cells of affine semigroups (non-shortcut letters).
   Pair (n, n+1): orientation '+': divide by the primes of n+1, multiply by those of n
   (D = +1, cycles >= 0);  orientation '-': divide by primes of n, multiply by primes of
   n+1 (D = -1, cycles <= 0).  A word is DETERMINISTIC-consistent if the multiplier is a
   single prime q and the word obeys: divide by the smallest available divisor prime
   whenever one divides x, else x -> q x + 1.
